-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software fetched at build time
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository does not contain the following; scripts/setup.sh downloads
them, and the boot and rootfs images the scripts build include them, each
under its own license:

  TECHO5 boot chain and tools      MIT
  Linux kernel (amazon-oss)        GPL-2.0
  MT7668 Wi-Fi driver (amazon-oss) Dual BSD/GPL, with some files marked
                                   MediaTek proprietary
  Alpine Linux and its packages    various (see each package)
  Arm GNU Toolchain                various (GPL-3.0 with exceptions, etc.)

Vendor modules and firmware are read from the user's own unit or LineageOS
zip during the build and are not distributed by this project.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Piper and its voice
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/build-piper.sh downloads Piper (piper-tts, libpiper: GPL-3.0) and the
libraries it loads (onnxruntime: MIT; abseil: Apache-2.0; protobuf, re2: BSD;
ICU; espeak-ng: GPL-3.0; libstdc++: GPL-3.0 with the runtime exception; musl:
MIT) from Alpine Linux's edge repositories, and the pt_BR "faber" voice from
https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices (dataset CC0, fine-tuned from the
en_US lessac voice, whose dataset has its own terms). The rootfs images the
scripts build include them; the repository does not.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Weather data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
penguin-weather fetches forecasts and place names, on the unit and at run
time, from Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com). Open-Meteo's data is licensed
under CC BY 4.0 (https://open-meteo.com/en/license): "Weather data by
Open-Meteo.com". None of it is part of this repository or of the images.
